                <pb facs="0797" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg717"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Buck to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo,
                                Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-05-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 642.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of instruction No. 399, of date April 12 last, relative to memoranda exchanged
                    between the Department of State and the British embassy at Washington on the
                    subject of the reference to arbitration of the question of the Japanese
                    Government’s right to the imposition of the house tax in respect of buildings
                    which are held under perpetual lease.</p>
                <p>The opinion of the Department, as set forth in the quotation from its memorandum
                    embodied in the instruction, is that “the scope of the reference should be such
                    as to include and settle all questions in controversy relative to the imposition
                    of charges and taxes of whatever style and character,” and I am instructed to
                    make proper representations to the Japanese Government in support of the view
                    that the question in all its bearings should be referred for final settlement by
                    the proposed arbitration.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to state that upon the receipt of the above instruction I
                    communicated the views of the Department to the Japanese minister for foreign
                    affairs in a note of date the 13th instant, copy of which is herewith
                    inclosed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. E. Buck.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d714-a1.xml" xpointer="d714-a1"/>
            </div>
